                        "entry_id": "f28c20da-481e-39f2-86e1-b52f821774b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An instance of fading away, of diminishing in proximity or intensity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd5b0980-0e1e-4072-8529-5fcb7d16418a",
                                "sense_id": "c99f86a8-8073-316f-b1f3-c6841e84108b",
                                "text": "In his final years he [John Ogdon] gave an interview to an American journalist who noticed that \"his handshake is a boneless fadeaway[\"]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "60d676a6-7ea5-3c42-baec-145852e7e0cb",
                        "entry_id": "f28c20da-481e-39f2-86e1-b52f821774b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A jump shot made while jumping backwards, away from the basket, with the goal to create space between the shooter and the defender, making it much harder to block."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a532491a-0152-4d05-8af2-0974eb59e165",
                                "sense_id": "60d676a6-7ea5-3c42-baec-145852e7e0cb",
                                "text": "He taunted the Knicks instead with hanging jumpers, impossible fadeaways and layups in traffic."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8bd4548a-e092-46d1-83e6-7d5177e6e64b",
                                "sense_id": "60d676a6-7ea5-3c42-baec-145852e7e0cb",
                                "text": "[Markieff] Morris isn’t quite the post-up threat that [Enes] Kanter is, and he can play both the 4 spot and 5 spot instead of just center, like Kanter. He is capable of playing a similar way, backing defenders down in the post. He prefers getting his buckets there with a bevy of fade-aways and jumpers. He’s a heat checker. And he can get hot on the block."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "93ac9465-fa34-3578-8311-8336837cf0ee",
                        "entry_id": "f28c20da-481e-39f2-86e1-b52f821774b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The ending of a personal relationship by stopping any contact with the other party and not providing an explanation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "026bd354-0b49-4d7d-888b-d7ef8ebd3967",
                                "sense_id": "93ac9465-fa34-3578-8311-8336837cf0ee",
                                "text": "Why some people choose to do the infamous \"fadeaway\" instead of a clean break?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
